  "body": "We built an app service that manages rooms for our users.\r\nThis service sets the power level of the members of chat groups.\r\n\r\nWe have a room with over 2000 persons in it and want to set the power level of each of these persons, so that only a few of them can write and most can only read. In our application the user can configure if a user can read or write.\r\n\r\nTo achieve that we use the botIntent like this: `botIntent.sendStateEvent(roomId, 'm.room.power_levels', '', eventContent);`\r\nThe eventContent contains all users and their power levels.\r\n\r\nIn this big group we get the following error: `M_TOO_LARGE: event too large`.\r\n\r\n[https://github.com/matrix-org/mjolnir/issues/129](Here) i read that there is an limit as of how big an event can be.\r\nSo is there no way to set power levels for so many persons in a chat room?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Homeserver\r\n\r\nchat.church.tools\r\n\r\n### Synapse Version\r\n\r\n{\"server_version\":\"1.80.0\",\"python_version\":\"3.8.10\"}\r\n\r\n### Installation Method\r\n\r\nDebian packages from packages.matrix.org\r\n\r\n### Database\r\n\r\nPostgreSQL",
